    headline: "Meet the stranger who has your voice",
    why: "You have never actually heard yourself. What you call \"your voice\" arrives through bone conduction — an internal, softened, flattering mix of skull and ear. Everyone else hears the air-conducted version: cheaper, sharper, and positioned differently. This is why recordings feel like an ambush. It is not vanity; the mismatch is physical. Until you close that gap with evidence, every improvement you attempt is guesswork.",
