    headline: "Space, not force",
    why: "Mumbling is almost never a volume problem. It is a space problem. Consonants are made by interrupting airflow with lips, tongue and jaw — and when the jaw is half-closed and the tongue is lazy, those interruptions blur into a single vowel soup. The fix is mechanical and immediate: open the mouth more than feels natural, and let air fill the chamber before you speak. Force produces shouting. Space produces clarity.",
