    example: {
      label: "One dial on one line",
      text: "Flat: \"We didn't hit the target this quarter and I want to talk about why.\" Dialled (pace down 30%, pitch down slightly): \"We didn't hit the target this quarter. — pause — I want to talk about why.\" Identical words. The second version buys you the room's full attention, because the tempo told them something serious was arriving.",
    },
    mistake: "Moving the projection dial to compensate for weakness in the others. Loud is not engaged — a fast, flat, loud speaker is simply harder to ignore and no easier to follow. Pause and pace do the heavy lifting; volume is the least interesting dial you own.",
