    headline: "The brakes you are pumping without knowing",
    why: "Fillers are not random. They appear at predictable moments: when you are thinking of the next word, when you are unsure whether your last sentence was acceptable, and when you are afraid of silence. That means they are not a vocabulary habit — they are a *management* habit. You are using sound to cover the gap where thinking happens. Remove the noise without fixing the reason and the gap gets filled with something else: speed, repetition, or apology.",
