    headline: "Silence makes other people lean in",
    why: "Robert Greene's fourth law — always say less than necessary — sounds like a style note and is actually a power mechanism. Speech is cheap; silence is expensive and therefore loaded. When you stop talking in a conversation, the other person must fill the gap, and whatever they fill it with tells you more than any question would. In negotiation, the first person to speak after a demand almost always concedes something.",
