    headline: "The structure that survives panic",
    why: "Under pressure, working memory drops to roughly one item. You cannot hold a five-part argument in your head while your heart is at 120 beats per minute — which is why intelligent people produce shapeless answers in interviews. The fix is a structure small enough to survive panic. PREP is four beats: Point, Reason, Example, Point. It fits in one hand, needs no paper, and works for anything from a toast to a hostile question.",
